-- Ingredient explainers (what it is / why used / hair effects) with cited sources.
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Plain purified water (Aqua). It is the base liquid of most shampoos, conditioners and styling products.', why_used='It dissolves other ingredients, carries them onto hair and scalp, and makes products spreadable and rinseable.', hair_effects='Water hydrates hair temporarily but does not condition on its own. It has no known irritation concern, though water-heavy formulas need preservatives to stay safe.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/water' where lower(name) in ('water', 'water (aqua)', 'aqua (water)');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Juice or gel from the inner leaf of the aloe vera plant, a water-based plant extract containing sugars and other plant compounds.', why_used='Added as a water-rich conditioning and moisturizing ingredient, often in gels and leave-ins.', hair_effects='May add light moisture and slip to hair and scalp. Rarely, plant extracts cause irritation or allergy, so people with plant sensitivities should patch test.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/aloe-barbadensis-leaf-juice' where lower(name) in ('aloe barbadensis leaf juice', 'aloe barbadensis leave juice (decolorized)');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A waxy fatty alcohol blend (cetyl and stearyl alcohol) made from plant or synthetic sources. Despite the name, it is not a drying alcohol like ethanol.', why_used='It thickens creams and conditioners, helps oil and water mix, and gives a smooth, soft feel.', hair_effects='It may soften hair and help it feel smoother and easier to detangle. Heavy use can cause buildup on fine hair, and rare scalp allergy is possible.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/cetearyl-alcohol' where lower(name) in ('cetearyl alcohol');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A waxy fatty alcohol, usually made from plant oils such as coconut or palm. Despite the name, it is not a drying alcohol like rubbing alcohol.', why_used='It thickens creams, stabilizes emulsions and softens hair as a conditioning ingredient.', hair_effects='It may make hair feel smoother and softer and help with detangling. Heavy use can weigh down fine hair, and rarely it may irritate very sensitive skin.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/cetyl-alcohol' where lower(name) in ('cetyl alcohol');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Stearyl alcohol is a waxy fatty alcohol, usually made from plant oils. It is not a drying alcohol like ethanol.', why_used='Used to thicken creams and help oil and water mix, and as a softening, conditioning agent in conditioners and masks.', hair_effects='May make hair feel softer and easier to detangle. It is generally well tolerated, though heavy use can feel coating on fine hair, and rare skin allergy is possible.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/stearyl-alcohol' where lower(name) in ('stearyl alcohol');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A synthetic preservative, related to a compound found naturally in green tea, that is a clear, slightly oily liquid.', why_used='It stops bacteria, yeast and mold from growing in water-based shampoos and conditioners so they stay safe to use.', hair_effects='It does nothing for hair itself. It is generally well tolerated at allowed levels, but may irritate sensitive or allergy-prone scalps in some people.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredients/phenoxyethanol' where lower(name) in ('phenoxyethanol', 'phenoxyethanol (optiphen nd)');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A catch-all label for a blend of scent chemicals, natural or synthetic. The exact ingredients usually are not listed individually.', why_used='It gives products a pleasant smell and can mask the odor of other ingredients.', hair_effects='It has no conditioning benefit for hair. Fragrance is a common cause of contact allergy and scalp irritation, so people with sensitive skin or known allergies may prefer fragrance-free products.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/products/weleda-rosemary-revitalising-hair-tonic' where lower(name) in ('fragrance', 'fragrance (parfum)');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A mild organic acid found in citrus fruits, usually made by fermentation for cosmetic use.', why_used='Used to adjust product pH toward the slightly acidic range of hair and scalp, and to help stabilize formulas.', hair_effects='A slightly acidic pH may help hair cuticles lie flatter, which can reduce frizz. At higher levels it can sting or irritate sensitive or broken scalp skin.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/citric-acid' where lower(name) in ('citric acid', 'citric acid');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A plant oil pressed from coconut meat, made mostly of saturated fats such as lauric acid.', why_used='It adds shine and softness, acts as a conditioning oil, and may reduce water absorption by hair.', hair_effects='It may help reduce protein loss and frizz and add shine. It can build up and feel heavy or stiff on fine or low-porosity hair, and people with coconut allergy should avoid it.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/cocos-nucifera-oil' where lower(name) in ('cocos nucifera (coconut) oil');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A synthetic, glycerin-based ingredient made from a fatty alcohol. It is a mild, clear liquid.', why_used='It helps preserve products by boosting other preservatives, and it also softens and moisturizes the skin.', hair_effects='It is generally well tolerated at typical use levels. Rarely, it may cause irritation or allergy on sensitive scalps.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/ethylhexylglycerin' where lower(name) in ('ethylhexylglycerin', 'ethylhexylglycerin');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Glycerin is a clear, sweet, syrupy liquid made from plant oils or animal fats. It is a humectant, meaning it attracts water.', why_used='Added to draw in and hold moisture and to make products feel smoother and easier to spread.', hair_effects='May help hair feel more hydrated and soft. In very dry air it can pull water out of hair and cause dryness or frizz in some people, and it is rarely irritating.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/glycerin' where lower(name) in ('glycerin', 'glycerin', 'glycerin (vegetable)');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Behentrimonium chloride (BTAC) is a synthetic, positively charged conditioning agent made from behenyl alcohol, a fatty alcohol from plants.', why_used='It sticks to negatively charged, damaged hair to detangle, soften and reduce static in conditioners and masks.', hair_effects='It may make hair smoother, softer and easier to comb. It can build up with heavy use and may irritate eyes or sensitive scalps, so rinse well.', info_source_url='https://www.cir-safety.org/ingredient/behentrimonium-chloride' where lower(name) in ('behentrimonium chloride');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Behentrimonium methosulfate is a conditioning agent made from a fatty alcohol from grapeseed oil, with a positive electric charge. It is often paired with cetyl or cetearyl alcohol.', why_used='It coats hair to detangle, smooth and reduce static, and it helps form conditioner creams.', hair_effects='It can leave hair soft and easy to comb. On fine or oily hair it may feel heavy or build up, and rarely it may irritate sensitive scalps.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/behentrimonium-methosulfate' where lower(name) in ('behentrimonium methosulfate (btms)', 'behentromonium methosulfate');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A creamy fat (butter) pressed from the nuts of the African shea tree, rich in fatty acids and unsaponifiable compounds.', why_used='Used as an emollient to soften, seal in moisture and add richness to conditioners and styling creams.', hair_effects='May reduce dryness and add softness, especially for coarse or curly hair. It can weigh down fine hair or build up, and people with tree-nut allergy should be cautious, though reactions are rare.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/butyrospermum-parkii-butter' where lower(name) in ('butyrospermum parkii (shea) butter');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Also called provitamin B5, it is a clear, sticky liquid or powder that the body can convert to pantothenic acid (vitamin B5).', why_used='It is a humectant that draws in and holds water, and it is used to add softness and moisture to hair products.', hair_effects='It may help hair feel softer, thicker and shinier by holding moisture and coating the strand. Irritation is uncommon, though rare skin sensitivity can occur.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/panthenol' where lower(name) in ('panthenol');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A small, glycerin-like molecule (an alkane diol) made from caprylic acid, found in coconut and palm oil or made synthetically.', why_used='It holds moisture and softens as a humectant, and it boosts the effect of preservatives in the formula.', hair_effects='It may help products feel less dry. It is generally considered well tolerated, though a small number of people with sensitive scalps could get mild irritation.', info_source_url='https://www.cir-safety.org/ingredient/caprylyl-glycol' where lower(name) in ('caprylyl glycol');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A liquid made by fermenting radish root with the bacterium Leuconostoc, then filtering out the cells.', why_used='Used as a naturally derived preservative to help keep water-based products from spoiling.', hair_effects='It has no known direct benefit for hair and is generally considered low irritation. Sensitive people could react to any preservative, so patch testing is reasonable.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/leuconostoc-radish-root-ferment-lysate-filtrate' where lower(name) in ('leuconostoc/radish root ferment filtrate');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Caprylic/capric triglyceride is a light, non-greasy oil made from coconut or palm oil fatty acids combined with glycerin.', why_used='It acts as a lightweight emollient and solvent that adds slip and softness and helps carry other ingredients.', hair_effects='It may soften hair and add light shine without a heavy feel. It is generally well tolerated, though it can still add some residue on very fine hair.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/caprylic-capric-triglyceride' where lower(name) in ('caprylic/capric triglyceride', 'caprylic/capric triglycerides');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A plant extract made from maple tree material, such as sap or bark. It contains sugars and plant compounds.', why_used='It is added as a humectant and conditioning ingredient, and is claimed to offer antioxidant benefits.', hair_effects='It may help hair hold some moisture, but evidence for hair-specific benefits is limited. Plant extracts can occasionally cause allergy, so patch test if you are sensitive.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/products/donnas-recipe-sweet-potato-pie-extra-creamy-hair-cream-2' where lower(name) in ('acer saccharum (sugar maple) extract');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Graviola extract comes from the soursop fruit tree (Annona muricata), a tropical plant extract.', why_used='Marketed as a botanical ingredient to add a plant-derived conditioning or antioxidant feel to hair products.', hair_effects='Hair benefits are not well documented, so any claims are unproven. Plant extracts can occasionally irritate skin, so people with sensitive scalps should patch test.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/products/camille-rose-guava-slip-shampoo' where lower(name) in ('annona muricata (graviola) fruit extract');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A simple acid found naturally in some plants and berries, and also made synthetically for use in products.', why_used='It is a preservative that helps stop microbes growing in water-based hair products, and can adjust pH.', hair_effects='It does not condition hair. It is considered safe at low levels, but may sting or irritate sensitive skin or an already irritated scalp.', info_source_url='https://www.cir-safety.org/sites/default/files/120_final_ba.pdf' where lower(name) in ('benzoic acid');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='An aromatic alcohol found naturally in some plants and also made synthetically. It is not a drying alcohol like ethanol.', why_used='It acts as a preservative, a solvent and a fragrance component.', hair_effects='It helps keep products free of microbes. It is a recognized fragrance allergen, so people prone to contact allergy or scalp irritation may react to it.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/benzyl-alcohol' where lower(name) in ('benzyl alcohol');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A synthetic or plant-derived ester of benzoic acid and benzyl alcohol, found naturally in some balsams and essential oils.', why_used='Used as a fragrance ingredient and solvent that helps hold scent, and sometimes as a fixative.', hair_effects='It does nothing for hair itself. It is a recognized fragrance allergen, so people with fragrance allergy or sensitive scalps may get irritation or rashes.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/benzyl-benzoate' where lower(name) in ('benzyl benzoate');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A synthetic fragrance ingredient with a faint sweet, floral scent, made from benzyl alcohol and salicylic acid.', why_used='It gives or fixes scent in shampoos and conditioners, and can help other fragrances last longer.', hair_effects='It has no known benefit for hair itself. It is a listed fragrance allergen, so people with fragrance allergies or a sensitive scalp may react to it.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/benzyl-salicylate' where lower(name) in ('benzyl salicylate');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Oil or oil-derived ingredients from rapeseed (canola) plant seeds. It is rich in fatty acids and plant sterols.', why_used='It softens and conditions as an emollient, and it is a source material for other conditioning ingredients.', hair_effects='It may add softness and shine and reduce dryness. Heavy oils can weigh down fine hair or build up, and allergy is uncommon.', info_source_url='https://www.cir-safety.org/sites/default/files/Phytos_092013_Rep.pdf' where lower(name) in ('brassica campestris (rapeseed) seed oil');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='An extract from sweet orange (Citrus aurantium dulcis) fruit, peel or flowers, containing plant acids, sugars and aromatic compounds.', why_used='Added for light scent, as a conditioning plant extract, or as a source of mild fruit acids.', hair_effects='May add a pleasant scent and a light conditioning feel. Citrus-derived ingredients can irritate sensitive scalps or cause allergic reactions in some people.', info_source_url='https://www.cir-safety.org/sites/default/files/cplant092016tent.pdf' where lower(name) in ('citrus aurantium dulcis (orange) fruit extract');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A plant extract made from lemon fruit, containing citrus acids, vitamin C and other plant compounds.', why_used='It is used to lower product pH, add a fresh scent, and as a plant-derived additive claimed to give clarifying effects.', hair_effects='Its acids may help remove residue and add shine by smoothing the cuticle. It can irritate or dry the scalp, and citrus can raise sun sensitivity on skin, so be cautious if sensitive.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/citrus-limon-fruit-extract' where lower(name) in ('citrus limon (lemon) fruit extract');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A mild cleansing agent (surfactant) made from coconut-derived fatty acids. It is amphoteric, meaning it can carry either charge.', why_used='It adds foam, thickens shampoos, and makes harsher cleansers gentler.', hair_effects='It cleans with less harshness than many stronger surfactants. Some people develop contact allergy to it or to impurities from manufacturing, so cautious use is advised for sensitive scalps.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/cocamidopropyl-betaine' where lower(name) in ('cocamidopropyl betaine');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A citrus-smelling aromatic compound found in orange and lemon peel oils, also made synthetically.', why_used='Used to give products a fresh citrus fragrance.', hair_effects='It adds scent but has no known hair benefit. It can oxidize into allergenic compounds, so people with fragrance allergies or sensitive scalps should be cautious.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/d-limonene' where lower(name) in ('d-limonene');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A mild cleansing agent (surfactant) made from sugars from corn or wheat and fatty alcohols from coconut or palm.', why_used='It creates foam and lifts dirt and oil in shampoos, and is often chosen as a gentler alternative to sulfates.', hair_effects='It may clean gently with less stripping, which can suit sensitive scalps. It can still dry hair for some people and cleans less strongly on heavy buildup.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/decyl-glucoside' where lower(name) in ('decyl glucoside', 'decyl glucoside');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A synthetic, colorless, nearly odorless liquid in the glycol family. It mixes with both water and oils.', why_used='It works as a solvent, helps dissolve fragrance, and thins and carries other ingredients.', hair_effects='It can help ingredients spread evenly and may attract some moisture. It is generally well tolerated, but rare scalp irritation or allergy is possible.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/dipropylene-glycol' where lower(name) in ('dipropylene glycol');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A mild, coconut-derived surfactant (amphoteric type) that has both positive and negative charges.', why_used='Used as a gentle cleanser and foam booster, often alongside stronger surfactants to make shampoos milder.', hair_effects='May clean while being less harsh on hair and scalp than many surfactants. Any surfactant can dry hair, and rare irritation or allergy is possible, particularly from impurities.', info_source_url='https://www.cir-safety.org/sites/default/files/Amphocarboxylates_1.pdf' where lower(name) in ('disodium cocoamphodipropionate');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='An extract from the horsetail plant (Equisetum arvense), an ancient plant rich in silica and plant compounds called flavonoids.', why_used='It is added as a botanical extract, often in products claimed to support hair strength or soothe the scalp.', hair_effects='It is claimed to strengthen hair, but good evidence is limited. Topical use is generally mild, though plant extracts can occasionally cause scalp allergy.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/equisetum-arvense-extract' where lower(name) in ('equisetum arvense (horsetail) extract');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Extracts or ingredients from seaweed or algae, which contain sugars, minerals and plant compounds. Exact contents vary by species.', why_used='It is added as a moisturizing, conditioning or film-forming ingredient, and is often marketed as soothing.', hair_effects='It may help hair hold moisture and feel softer, though the evidence is limited. People with seaweed or iodine sensitivities may want to be cautious.', info_source_url='https://www.cir-safety.org/sites/default/files/Red%20Algae.pdf' where lower(name) in ('gellidiela acerosa (algae) extract');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='An ester made from glycerin and caprylic acid, a fatty acid found in coconut and palm oils.', why_used='Used as a mild emollient and emulsifier, and to boost the effect of preservatives.', hair_effects='May add softness and help products stay stable. It is generally well tolerated, though rare skin irritation is possible in sensitive people.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/glyceryl-caprylate' where lower(name) in ('glyceryl caprylate');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A plant oil pressed from soybeans, rich in unsaturated fatty acids such as linoleic acid.', why_used='It acts as an emollient that softens hair and adds slip, shine and moisture in conditioners and styling creams.', hair_effects='It may soften hair and reduce frizz. It can feel heavy or greasy on fine hair, and people with soy allergy should be cautious, though refined oil has little protein.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/products/africas-best-ultimate-herbal-oil' where lower(name) in ('glycine soja (soybean) oil');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A modified guar gum, from guar beans, given a positive charge. It is a conditioning polymer.', why_used='It sticks to hair to reduce tangles and static, and it helps conditioning shampoos work.', hair_effects='It may make hair easier to comb and smoother. It can build up over time, especially on fine hair, which a clarifying shampoo can remove.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/hydroxypropyl-guar-hydroxypropyltrimonium-chloride' where lower(name) in ('guar hydroxypropyltrimonium chloride');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='An extract from hibiscus flowers, a water or glycerin-based plant extract containing sugars, acids and pigments.', why_used='Added as a botanical conditioning ingredient, often with a marketing role for its plant origin and mild color.', hair_effects='May add a little softness or slip. Its hair benefits are modest and not well proven, and plant extracts can occasionally irritate sensitive scalps.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/hibiscus-sabdariffa-flower-extract' where lower(name) in ('hibiscus rosa-sinensis flower extract');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A sweet natural substance made by bees from flower nectar, mostly sugars with small amounts of enzymes and other compounds.', why_used='It is a humectant that draws water into hair and skin, and is used as a natural conditioning ingredient.', hair_effects='It may help hair feel softer and more moisturized. It can leave hair sticky if overused, and people with bee product or pollen allergy should avoid it.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/products/ors-shea-butter-honey-curly-coil-rich-style-cream' where lower(name) in ('honey', 'honey (mel)');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A starch-derived carbohydrate, commonly made from corn, wheat or potato. It is a white, water-soluble powder.', why_used='It acts as a binder, film former and texture or carrier ingredient.', hair_effects='It may add light hold or body as a film on hair. It is generally low-risk, but it can leave a sticky feel or buildup, and it is not meant as a conditioner.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/maltodextrin' where lower(name) in ('maltodextrin');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Neem oil or extract comes from the seeds and leaves of the neem tree, a plant native to South Asia.', why_used='Used as a plant oil or extract for conditioning, and traditionally associated with scalp care.', hair_effects='May moisturize hair, though evidence for scalp benefits is limited. It has a strong smell and can irritate or cause allergy in some people, so patch test first.', info_source_url='https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK234637' where lower(name) in ('melia azadirachta (neem) seed oil');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A plant oil pressed from olives, rich in oleic acid, a heavier unsaturated fatty acid.', why_used='It is an emollient that softens hair, adds shine, and seals in moisture in conditioners and oils.', hair_effects='It may add softness, shine and slip, especially on thick or dry hair. It can feel heavy and cause buildup on fine hair, and rarely irritates the scalp.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/olea-europaea-fruit-oil' where lower(name) in ('olea europaea (olive) fruit oil', 'olea europea (olive) fruit oil');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Polyquaternium-10 is a positively charged polymer made from modified cellulose, a plant fiber.', why_used='It conditions hair, reduces static and tangling, and thickens and stabilizes formulas.', hair_effects='It deposits on hair to improve combing and smoothness. It can build up over time, especially on fine hair, and irritation is rare.', info_source_url='https://www.cir-safety.org/ingredient/polyquaternium-10' where lower(name) in ('polyquaternium-10', 'polyquaternium-10');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Polyquaternium-7 is a synthetic, positively charged polymer used in many personal care products.', why_used='Used as a conditioning and anti-static agent because it sticks to negatively charged, damaged hair.', hair_effects='May reduce static and make hair easier to comb. With repeated use it can build up and weigh hair down, and it is generally considered low in irritation.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/polyquaternium-7' where lower(name) in ('polyquaternium-7');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A natural plant carbohydrate found in fruit such as apples and citrus peel, which forms a gel in water.', why_used='It thickens products and forms a light film, so it is used in stylers and dry shampoos for hold and body.', hair_effects='It may add light hold, body and a smoother feel. Too much can leave hair stiff or sticky, and it is generally well tolerated.', info_source_url='https://www.cir-safety.org/sites/default/files/plpogu092015final.pdf' where lower(name) in ('pectin');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A plant oil pressed from avocado fruit, rich in fatty acids such as oleic acid and containing some plant sterols.', why_used='It is an emollient that softens hair and skin, and it is used in conditioners and hair creams.', hair_effects='It may add softness, shine and slip, and help reduce dryness. Rich oils can weigh down fine hair or cause buildup, and people with avocado or latex-related allergies should be careful.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/persea-gratissima-oil' where lower(name) in ('persea gratissima (avocado) oil', 'persea gratissimia (avocado) oil', 'persea gratissima (organic avocado) oil');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Propanediol is a clear, odorless liquid glycol, often made from corn sugar. It is related to propylene glycol.', why_used='Used as a solvent, humectant and texture improver, and to help preservatives work.', hair_effects='May add moisture and a smooth feel. It is generally well tolerated, though rare skin irritation or allergy can occur.', info_source_url='https://www.cir-safety.org/sites/default/files/Tromet_092013_Rep.pdf' where lower(name) in ('propanediol');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='An extract from the fruit of the guava tree (Psidium guajava), containing vitamin C, sugars and plant antioxidants.', why_used='It is added as a fruity botanical extract, claimed to offer antioxidant and conditioning benefits.', hair_effects='It may offer mild antioxidant and softening effects, but hair-specific evidence is limited. It is generally mild, though plant extracts can occasionally irritate sensitive scalps.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/psidium-guajava-fruit-extract' where lower(name) in ('psidium guajava (guava) fruit extract');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A thick vegetable oil pressed from castor beans. It is high in ricinoleic acid.', why_used='It adds slip, shine and moisture-holding feel, and it thickens and softens in balms and conditioners.', hair_effects='It may help coat hair and make it feel softer and glossier. It is heavy and sticky, so it can weigh hair down, and rare skin allergy is possible. Claims about hair growth are not well proven.', info_source_url='https://www.cir-safety.org/sites/default/files/Castor%20Oil.pdf' where lower(name) in ('ricinus communis (castor) seed oil');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='An essential oil steam-distilled from rosemary leaves, containing strongly scented plant compounds.', why_used='Used for fragrance and as a plant ingredient in scalp tonics and shampoos.', hair_effects='It is claimed to support scalp care, but evidence is limited. It can irritate skin and contains fragrance allergens such as limonene, so sensitive people should be cautious.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/rosmarinus-officinalis-leaf-oil' where lower(name) in ('rosmarinus officinalis (rosemary) leaf oil');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='The sodium salt of acetic acid (the acid in vinegar), a simple, water-soluble white salt.', why_used='It works as a pH buffer that keeps a product''s acidity steady, often alongside acids such as acetic or citric acid.', hair_effects='It does not directly condition hair, but helps keep products at a hair-friendly pH. It is generally considered low risk, with irritation uncommon.', info_source_url='https://www.cir-safety.org/sites/default/files/Hyaluronates_1.pdf' where lower(name) in ('sodium acetate');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='An extract from the sugarcane plant (Saccharum officinarum). It contains sugars and may include plant acids.', why_used='It is used as a humectant, conditioning and skin-softening ingredient.', hair_effects='It may help hair hold some moisture. Evidence for hair benefits is limited, and sugar-rich extracts can feel sticky. Irritation is uncommon, but plant extracts can occasionally trigger allergy.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/saccharum-officinarum-extract' where lower(name) in ('saccharum officinarum (sugarcane) extract');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A plant oil pressed from sesame seeds, made mostly of fatty acids.', why_used='Used as an emollient to soften and add shine, and to help seal in moisture.', hair_effects='May make hair feel softer and less dry. It can feel heavy on fine hair, and people with sesame allergy should avoid it.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/sesamum-indicum-seed-oil' where lower(name) in ('sesamum indicum (sesame) seed oil');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A liquid wax, not a true oil, pressed from jojoba plant seeds, with a structure similar to the skin''s natural sebum.', why_used='It is an emollient that adds shine and softness and helps seal in moisture in hair oils and conditioners.', hair_effects='It may soften hair, add shine and feel light on the scalp. It can build up on very fine hair, and rare allergic reactions are possible.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/products/pump-miracle-curl-oil' where lower(name) in ('simmondsia chinensis (jojoba) seed oil', 'simmondsia chinesis (jojoba) seed oil', 'simmondsia chinensis (organic jojoba) seed oil');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Also called lye, a strong alkaline chemical made industrially. In cosmetics it is used in tiny amounts and is largely neutralized in the finished product.', why_used='It adjusts pH and helps make some soaps and thickened formulas, and it is also used in hair relaxers.', hair_effects='At the small amounts used in shampoos it is balanced to a safe pH. At high strength, such as in relaxers, it can swell and damage hair and burn skin, so follow directions carefully.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/products/head-shoulders-pro-expert-shampoo-hair-fall-defence' where lower(name) in ('sodium hydroxide');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A protein from silkworm cocoons, usually broken into smaller pieces (hydrolyzed) so it dissolves in water.', why_used='Used to add smoothness and shine and to help form a light film on hair.', hair_effects='May make hair feel smoother and look shinier. It can build up or make hair feel stiff in people sensitive to protein, and may be unsuitable for those with silk allergy.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/products/sheamoisture-coconut-hibiscus-curl-style-milk-with-silk-protein-neem-oil-for-thick-defined-curly-hair' where lower(name) in ('sodium lauroyl hydrolyzed silk');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A group of mild emulsifiers (such as sodium stearoyl lactylate) made by combining fatty acids with lactic acid.', why_used='They help oil and water blend and keep creams and conditioners stable and smooth.', hair_effects='They may help give a soft, smooth feel and are generally mild. They can add some residue with heavy use, and irritation is uncommon.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/products/living-proof-full-shampoo-uk' where lower(name) in ('sodium lauroyl lactylate');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A mild cleansing agent (surfactant) made from an amino-acid-like building block, sarcosine, joined to fatty acids such as coconut. Examples include sodium lauroyl sarcosinate.', why_used='It cleans, creates foam and is used in gentler shampoos and washes.', hair_effects='It is generally considered milder than harsh sulfates and may leave hair feeling soft. Any cleanser can dry hair or irritate sensitive scalps, so use it with a conditioner if hair feels dry.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/products/living-proof-full-shampoo-uk' where lower(name) in ('sodium lauroyl sarcosinate');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Kakadu plum is an Australian fruit whose extract or oil is rich in vitamin C and other plant compounds.', why_used='Added as a botanical antioxidant and conditioning ingredient.', hair_effects='Its effects on hair are not well studied, so benefits are mainly claimed. Plant extracts can occasionally irritate sensitive scalps, so patch testing is sensible.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/products/sweet-chemistry-elasticity-reinforcing-lipid-cream' where lower(name) in ('terminala ferdinandiana (kakadu plum) fruit extract');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Vitamin E, a fat-soluble antioxidant found in plant oils and also made synthetically.', why_used='It protects oils and other ingredients from going rancid and may help condition hair and skin.', hair_effects='It may help protect the product and lightly soften hair. It is usually well tolerated, though rare scalp allergy can occur, and it can feel heavy at high levels.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/tocopherol' where lower(name) in ('tocopherol');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='A synthetic liquid made from citric acid, the acid found in citrus fruit, combined with ethanol.', why_used='It is used as a plasticizer that keeps film-forming polymers flexible, and as a solvent and fragrance fixative.', hair_effects='It may help styling products feel less stiff. It is generally considered low-risk, though rare irritation or allergy is possible on sensitive skin.', info_source_url='https://www.cosmeticsinfo.org/ingredient/citric-acid' where lower(name) in ('triethyl citrate');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Linseed (flax seed) oil is a plant oil rich in omega-3 fatty acids such as alpha-linolenic acid.', why_used='Used as an emollient oil to soften and add shine to hair products.', hair_effects='May add softness and shine. It can go rancid and smell off, feel heavy on fine hair, and rarely cause irritation.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/ingredients/linum-usitatissimum-seed-oil' where lower(name) in ('unum ustiatissium (linseed) oil extract');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='An extract from the stinging nettle plant (Urtica dioica), containing minerals, plant acids and other plant compounds.', why_used='It is added as a botanical extract, claimed to soothe the scalp and support hair condition.', hair_effects='It is claimed to condition hair and calm the scalp, but good evidence is limited. Extracts are generally mild, though plant allergies or sensitive scalps may react.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/products/giovanni-direct-leave-in-conditioner' where lower(name) in ('urtica dioica (nettle) leaf extract');
update public.ingredients set what_it_is='Xanthan gum is a natural thickener made by bacteria fermenting sugar. It is a long, water-loving carbohydrate molecule.', why_used='It thickens products, keeps ingredients evenly mixed and gives gels and curl creams a smoother texture.', hair_effects='It may give light hold and body in styling products. Too much can feel sticky or flaky, and irritation is rare.', info_source_url='https://incidecoder.com/products/bigen-permanent-hair-color-59-oriental-black' where lower(name) in ('xanthan gum');
